 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "logs is a list of [taskName, action, timestamp] string rows on a single CPU, with action \"enter\" or \"exit\" and canonical decimal timestamps in non-decreasing order. Tasks nest like a call stack: an \"enter\" pauses the running task, the matching \"exit\" closes the innermost open task (same name) and resumes the one below. Every entered task is exited by the end. Time is half-open: between consecutive events at times a <= b, the task on top of the stack (if any) runs for b - a units. Return [taskName, exclusiveTime] for every task name that appears, summed over all its runs, sorted by name in code-point order.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk09-a-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
